Relevant columns, usage, and typical conditions  
• boroname: filter the borough → WHERE boroname = 'Bronx'  
• health: classify tree health → WHERE health = 'Good' (or other values)  
• tree_id / idx: counting individual trees → COUNT(*)  
No other tables are needed.

```sql
--Description: 1) Which borough names exist in the data set?
SELECT DISTINCT "boroname"
FROM "trees"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Which health labels exist?
SELECT DISTINCT "health"
FROM "trees"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Look at a handful of Bronx rows to verify values
SELECT *
FROM "trees"
WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) How many trees are recorded in total?
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "all_trees"
FROM "trees";
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Tree counts by borough
SELECT "boroname",
       COUNT(*) AS "trees_per_borough"
FROM "trees"
GROUP BY "boroname"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Total number of trees in the Bronx
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "bronx_total"
FROM "trees"
WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx';
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Total number of Bronx trees whose health = 'Good'
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "bronx_good"
FROM "trees"
WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx'
  AND "health" = 'Good';
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Break‑down of Bronx trees by health status
SELECT "health",
       COUNT(*) AS "bronx_health_count"
FROM "trees"
WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx'
GROUP BY "health"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Compute the percentage of Good‑health trees in the Bronx (explicit formula)
SELECT 100.0 *
       SUM(CASE WHEN "health" = 'Good' THEN 1 END) /
       COUNT(*) AS "pct_good_bronx"
FROM "trees"
WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx';
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final answer—percentage of trees in the Bronx with a health status of Good
SELECT ROUND(
         100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "health" = 'Good' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) 
               / COUNT(*), 
         2
       ) AS "percentage_good_bronx"
FROM "trees"
WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx';
```
